@startuml
!define RECTANGLE class

RECTANGLE "Client Browser" as client {
  [User Interface]
  [Search Input Field]
  [Suggestions List]
}

RECTANGLE "Web Server (Node.js)" as server {
  [HTTP Request/Response]
  [Router]
  [Home Page Handler]
  [Static Asset Handler]
  [Search Handler]
  [Not Found Handler]
}

RECTANGLE "Modules" as modules {
  [Frontend Helpers]
  [Autocomplete Algorithm]
  [Data Access Layer]
}

RECTANGLE "Data Sources" as data {
  [Laureate JSON Data]
  [Public Assets Directory]
}

client --> server : HTTP Requests
server --> client : HTTP Responses

server --> modules : Delegates Processing
modules --> data : Reads/Writes

[Router] --> [Home Page Handler] : Routes "/"
[Router] --> [Search Handler] : Routes URLs with "search"
[Router] --> [Static Asset Handler] : Routes other URLs
[Search Handler] --> [Autocomplete Algorithm] : Processes Search
[Autocomplete Algorithm] --> [Data Access Layer] : Gets Laureate Names
[Data Access Layer] --> [Laureate JSON Data] : Reads Data
[Static Asset Handler] --> [Public Assets Directory] : Serves Files
[Home Page Handler] --> [Public Assets Directory] : Serves Home Page

note right of server
  System Constraints:
  - JavaScript/CommonJS environment
  - Filesystem reads from public directory
  - URL substring matching for search routing
  - Heroku deployment compatible
end note

note right of modules
  Non-Functional Requirements:
  - Modular separation of concerns
  - Automated testing coverage
  - Explicit media type mapping
end note

note right of data
  Data Requirements:
  - Laureate names as search domain
  - Local JSON data source
  - Static assets: HTML, CSS, JS, JPG, ICO
end note
@enduml
